```c
if (key_cpu >= nr_cpumask_bits || !cpu_possible(key_cpu))
```
Reason:
This fix adds an explicit check to ensure that `key_cpu` is within the valid range defined by `nr_cpumask_bits` before calling `cpu_possible()`. This prevents the spurious warning by ensuring that only valid CPU indices are processed, thus addressing the root cause of the issue.


